properties.description:
A declared list of every relation reflow2 derives: its rule, primitive reading, deduced or induced, and computing code. A test fails on drift in either direction. A served read evaluates the list over the open design. Planned by the 2026-09-29 fix program; it builds on the edge readings of PR #621.

SHIPPED 2026-09-29 in reflow2 PR #631 (squash 6329079). It includes:
- schema/derived/relations.yaml, declaring 23 relations: 3 stated fully over the readings, 19 partly, and 1 reading no edge;
- a core test holding each declaration to the edges its code reads;
- `derived_report`, which counts 22 of 23. The impact closure is declared but not counted.

Its change record, chg:reflow2-declares-its-derived-relations-and-serves-a-read-that-runs-them, and its passing check, ver:derived-relations-are-declared-checked-against-the-code-and-served (MCP tests observed failing 3 of 3 on origin/main 72917f6 first), are in main's committed export, NOT in this live store.

NOT YET DELIVERED:
- evaluating the declared RULES rather than the existing code;
- a rule-level check, which needs the planned rule engine;
- the closure count.

The status here stays `planned` on purpose: setting it to realized with no passing check in THIS store would be an unproven claim. The live store will reflect the delivery when main's records are folded in (ver:an-overlay-folds-after-a-squash-merge). The live server also still runs 0.74.0.

EXTENDED 2026-09-29, SHIPPED in reflow2 PR #633 (squash 26b1ed2), on top of #631: the check now starts from populations the declarations do not choose. A transitive walk from every declared function (any depth, all call forms, const tables, never into a writer); every edge-naming function in reflow2-core is declared or listed in schema/derived/edge_readers.yaml (132 `unjudged`, a count that may only shrink); components must be exactly the primitives the composition writes. Its passing check ver:derived-declarations-are-held-to-the-code-they-reach-the-crate-and-their-rule is in main's committed export, not this live store. Status left `planned` for the same reason as above. The NOT YET DELIVERED list above still stands.
